@startuml
' Figure 7.9 – System sequence diagram: uploading and ingesting a reference document
' Sprint 9 (FR-84). Sources: DocumentsService.presign/register/retry and
' DocumentIngestionService.ingest in src/documents/.
' The companion of fig-5-8: a second background pipeline, for a second corpus.
!include ../_style.puml
mainframe interaction SequenceDiagram Document ingestion
autonumber "0 :"

participant "Writer" as R
participant "System" as A
participant "Object\nstorage" as S
participant "Worker" as K
participant "Embedding\nprovider" as E
participant "Database" as D

ref over R, D : Sign in

R -> A : POST /documents/presign with the filename
activate A
A -> A : Accept PDF, DOCX, TXT or MD only
A --> R : Presigned upload URL and storage key
deactivate A
R -> S : PUT the file to the private documents bucket
activate S
S --> R : Stored
deactivate S

R -> A : POST /documents with the storage key
activate A
A -> S : Check the object exists and is under 10 MB
activate S
S --> A : Size
deactivate S
group One database transaction, under a per-writer lock
  A -> D : Count the writer's documents
  activate D
  alt already 20 documents
    A --> R : 409, the library is full
  else room left
    A -> D : Insert the document, status pending
    D --> A : Row
  end
  deactivate D
end
A -> K : Queue ingest-document
A --> R : The document, shown as pending
deactivate A

K -> D : Set the status to extracting
activate K
activate D
K -> S : Read the file
activate S
S --> K : Bytes
deactivate S
K -> K : Extract the text page by page

alt over 200 pages, or no text layer to read
  K -> D : Set the status to failed, with a readable reason
else text extracted
  K -> K : Split into chunks, keeping each chunk's page
  K -> E : Embed the chunks
  activate E
  E --> K : One vector per chunk
  deactivate E
  K -> D : In one transaction, replace the chunks\nand set the status to ready, with the page count
end
deactivate D
deactivate K

R -> A : GET /documents (the list polls while a row is in progress)
activate A
A --> R : Ready, or failed with its reason
deactivate A

opt the document failed
  R -> A : POST /documents/:id/retry
  activate A
  A -> D : Set the status back to pending
  A -> K : Queue ingest-document again
  A --> R : Pending
  deactivate A
end

note over R, D
  The file never passes through the api: the browser puts it straight
  into the private bucket. The bucket has no anonymous read policy, so
  the file is served back only through GET /documents/:id/file, as a
  10-minute presigned URL for its owner.
end note
@enduml
